const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Do I need an account to play Akari?',
    a: 'No. Everything works without signing in. Your current level, lives and board are auto-saved in your browser\'s local storage (kept for 24 hours), so a refresh or a closing tab doesn\'t lose your game.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why won\'t my cat place, or why did I lose a life?',
    a: 'Placing it broke a rule: too many cats around a numbered wall, or two cats facing each other along a row/column with no wall between. The toast tells you which one. Remove the cat and try another cell.',
  },
  {
    q: 'I\'m stuck. What do I do?',
    a: 'Press Hint — it\'s free and unlimited here. It always points at a cell that is correct in the final solution. Two wrong moves in a row make the button pulse.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does the ✗ mark do?',
    a: 'Classic Akari solvers mark cells that must stay empty. Double-click (or right-click on desktop, long-press on mobile) toggles it. It\'s a memory aid — the game doesn\'t count it as a move.',
